WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.350
Record capture reads the run's files, checks each image's checksum, and moves approved records to captured.

00:07.330 --> 00:14.880
The gallery shows every capture in the run side by side, so a reviewer can reject a bad shot before it reaches Figma.

00:14.860 --> 00:21.510
Record Figma stores where each capture lives: the file, the run page, and the frame's node ID.

00:21.490 --> 00:27.865
Each screenshot gets its own frame, so its node ID is a stable address for later exports.

00:27.845 --> 00:38.470
Both records now point at frames on one Figma page per run. This footage is the 0.16.0 run; the 0.20.0 run follows the same steps.
